          "text": "## Primary solution\n\nThe pattern indexes as a **rhombohedrally distorted, Nb-ordered thiospinel** in space group **\\(R\\bar{3}m\\) (No. 166), hexagonal setting**. The low-angle splitting is diagnostic:\n\n| hkl | Observed 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | Calculated 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 101 | 14.78 | 14.77 |\n| 003 | 15.22 | 15.22 |\n| 012 | 17.20 | 17.21 |\n| 110 | 24.14 | 24.14 |\n| 104 | 24.70 | 24.71 |\n| 021 | 28.42 | 28.42 |\n| 113 | 28.66 | 28.66 |\n| 015 | 29.15 | 29.15 |\n| 024 | 34.82 | 34.81 |\n\nRefined lattice parameters are approximately \\(a=7.3675\\) \u00c5 and \\(c=17.4470\\) \u00c5. Nb occupies the unique quarter of the octahedral sublattice, while Cr occupies the remaining three quarters. The internal coordinates below are a chemically regularized powder solution; their precision is lower than that of the unit cell and they should be finalized by Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_Ag2Cr3NbS8_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Indexed from Cu Kalpha1 powder data; ordered-spinel constrained solution'\n\n_chemical_name_common\n'niobium-ordered rhombohedral silver chromium thiospinel'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Ag2Cr3NbS8'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Ag2 Cr3 Nb S8'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               3\n\n_cell_length_a                      7.3675\n_cell_length_b                      7.3675\n_cell_length_c                     17.4470\n_cell_angle_alpha                  90\n_cell_angle_beta                   90\n_cell_angle_gamma                 120\n_cell_volume                      820.16\n\n_space_group_crystal_system        trigonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt          'R -3 m'\n_space_group_IT_number             166\n_space_group_setting               'hexagonal'\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe            x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type             'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength       1.5406\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn      4.38\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nAg  1\nCr  3\nNb  5\nS  -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nAg1 Ag  6 c  0.0000  0.0000  0.1219  1.0\nNb1 Nb  3 b  0.0000  0.0000  0.5000  1.0\nCr1 Cr  9 e  0.5000  0.0000  0.0000  1.0\nS1  S   6 c  0.0000  0.0000  0.2600  1.0\nS2  S  18 h  0.1800 -0.1800  0.0800  1.0\n```\n\nThis model gives sensible approximate coordination distances: Ag\u2013S \u2248 2.4 \u00c5 and Cr/Nb\u2013S \u2248 2.47\u20132.48 \u00c5. A polar \\(R3m\\) description is formally difficult to exclude from ordinary powder intensities, but no symmetry-breaking feature requires it; the centrosymmetric \\(R\\bar{3}m\\) model is therefore the preferred structure.",
